            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Jenny I"
            },
            "reviewBody": "soooo good.. made for a dinner party and everyone loved it! I used roasted pecans, pom, red onion and feta cheese. I made a dressing ( balsamic with honey, salt and pepper...mixed well then add a bit of olive oil ) and it was great with it! Plus be sure you dont drain the pom seeds and add the juice on top of the salad! Yummy!!"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Galegrover"
            },
            "reviewBody": "This was a great recipe. I didn't have any sprouts so I omitted them. I added bacon instead. I chopped 4 strips of bacon and then added red wine vinegar to pan after the bacon was crisp. I then let the vinegar dissipate to about half the original amount and poured it over the salad. The heat from the dressing blended very nicely with the feta and gave the dressing a creamy quality. I will definitely be making this again!",
            "datePublished": "2014-11-05T07:10:55.700Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Mia"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I made this pretty salad for Christmas dinner. I used 15 oz of spinach, soaked the red onion slices in ice water for 15 minutes (to mellow them out), dressed the salad (using a balsamic vinaigrette recipe from this site, and then plated it. Delicious!",
            "datePublished": "2016-12-26T16:08:06.173Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "tpf2005"
            },
            "reviewBody": "this was a hit in our house!! i think you could serve it with or without the feta, but i'm not a big fan of feta cheese. i served my salad with a homemade vinaigrette which i based off of \"balsamic vinaigrette\" on this site. Mix together the following ingredients and let sit for a little while to allow flavors to work together: 1/2 cup extra virgin olive oil, 1/2 cup balsamic vinegar, 1 clove crushed garlic, 1 tsp ground mustard, 1 pinch salt, black pepper to taste, and 3 TB honey",
            "datePublished": "2011-03-10T12:09:51.550Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Paul H"
            },
            "reviewBody": "This salad was excellent, I made it to go along with our Christmas Eve dinner. For the vinagirette I used juice and zest from a half a lemon, 3 TBL of red wine vinegar, 1 TBL of honey and 3 TBL of olive oil. Seeding the pomegranate was pretty easy. I just quartered it and then inverted each quarter and the seeds easily popped out. Everyone loved it.",
            "datePublished": "2009-12-30T05:26:56.363Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "4"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Marbear"
            },
            "reviewBody": "It turned out that pomegranates aren't in season anymore, so I replaced the pomegranates with blackberries and raspberries. I brought this to a potluck and it went over pretty well.",
            "datePublished": "2014-03-06T09:05:08.053Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "km88"
            },
            "reviewBody": "This salad is delicious, filling &amp; beautiful! DEFINITELY toast the walnuts first. Simple- five minutes on the stovetop with a touch of oil, &amp; so worth it. And I also made a balsamic vinegar/honey/oil mix for dressing, with a touch of salt &amp; pepper. I will make this many times in the future- I really enjoyed it!!",
            "datePublished": "2009-11-23T17:20:25.380Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "loddiecheftress"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I toast the walnuts first. The best dressing for this is if you can find pomegranate molasses and whisk in some EVOO, little sugar and a dash of S &amp; P. You can also buy pomegranate seeds already cleaned and ready at Trader Joes!",
            "datePublished": "2010-01-20T13:58:02.680Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "SneakyTongs8230"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I used arugula instead of spinach. One note- if you are making it ahead of time, don't toss with the dressing until read to serve!",
            "datePublished": "2025-12-10T23:21:48.318Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Peg"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Delightful flavor and so pretty! Served at Thanksgiving with a Balsamic, honey vinaigrette-everyone commented and requested the recipe. No sprouts and I used candied pecan bits (salad toppings in the produce section). Used POMS and now I've been requested to do for a wedding for 100! Really like this fresh, new salad!",
            "datePublished": "2016-03-03T16:07:16.610Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "cmach"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I made only enough for-myself so 1/4 recipe to go along with dinner. I bought the pomegranate seeds in a cup rather than a fresh pomegranate. I didn’t use sprouts and I added a bit of the pomegranate juice to my store bought balsamic vinaigrette dressing and it was delightful! Thank you!",
            "datePublished": "2024-01-15T14:38:10.547Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Gina Sanchez"
            },
            "reviewBody": "My Girlfriend made this years ago for a large family Christmas party that I helped her with one night before Santa Claus came to visit. Abby blew this gathering out of the water! Or maybe a snow castle. This was the first time I had it, I joined the 30 friends and family at a beautifully dressed up dining room table. But the Salad along side warm bread and a big slice of pasta, this Salad was the hit of all the food we served this night. It is so worth making the dressing a few days earlier or throwing it together that night. But you gotta try it! Enjoy Gina from California",
            "datePublished": "2026-05-10T00:51:21.564Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
